Z||000006||rogergarrison||12-08-2001||05:40 AM||||I wouldnt expect any 'big' gains. Not much of a 'performance' package, just a stroker kit for 2.8. So all you really add is cubes, and not that many. Youd be better off ordering the crank, getting a special grind cam, stronger rods & pistons, porting & polishing.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fiero_24||12-08-2001||11:12 AM||||Supposedly 180hp, but I am not sure.  I had some extra work done on the heads of my motor for a little more HP.  Yes there is a gain.  You also do the heads too.  The compression ratio is upped a little for a bigger bang, and you have the performance cam.  All that equals a big enough gain from the stock 140 range.  I will be leaving in a few minutes to do the final work.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||1
